      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Another way of thinking of this:  what most creators need to do is to split up \"who can initiate the action\" and \"who can see the action\".  Right now it is easy to gate the initiator by enabling/disabling the game object.  The receiver is gated by the broadcast type in the trigger.  By making the receivers not get the broadcast, you have linked these two independent cases.  The broadcasts should be absolute.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
